\ ==== the high-pass filter: :high-pass ====

\ A patch with :high-pass runs each voice, after the ladder, through a
\ two-pole Butterworth high-pass (the RBJ cookbook biquad at Q = 1/sqrt 2,
\ transposed direct form II). Without :high-pass there is none. The source is
\ a fixed-frequency sine; levels are in dB against the same sine unfiltered.

11 seed

: level-at ( hz patch -- a )
	| hz patch |
	patch :filtered instrument-patch! silence-audio
	:a4 1 :filtered note-on 1 render-audio 9600 48000 0 1 submatrix 48000 hz amplitude-at ;
: loss ( hz cutoff -- db )
	| hz cutoff |
	hz { :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz hz } ] :high-pass cutoff } level-at
	hz { :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz hz } ] } level-at / log10 20 * 100 * round 100 / ;

\ === the Butterworth response around a 1 kHz cutoff ===
250 1000 loss . 500 1000 loss . cr                               \ -24.12 -12.32 (12 dB per octave below)
1000 1000 loss . cr                                              \ -3.01 (3 dB down at the cutoff)
2000 1000 loss . 4000 1000 loss . cr                             \ -0.26 -0.02 (unity well above)
clear

\ === the response follows the cutoff ===
3500 7000 loss . 7000 7000 loss . cr                             \ -13.22 -3.01 (an octave below 7 kHz the bilinear warp makes the ratio tan(pi 3500/48000)/tan(pi 7000/48000) = 0.473, not 0.5)
clear

\ === a patch without :high-pass is not filtered ===
{ :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 100 } ] } :filtered instrument-patch! silence-audio
:a4 1 :filtered note-on 1 render-audio 9600 48000 0 1 submatrix 48000 100 amplitude-at 0.70710678 / 1000 * round 1000 / . cr   \ 1
clear

\ === white noise through it keeps its treble and loses its bass ===
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :white } ] :high-pass 7000 } :filtered instrument-patch! silence-audio
:a4 1 :filtered note-on 1 render-audio 0 @j 9600 13696 0 1 submatrix 4096 hann * fft magnitudes to bins
bins 170 341 0 1 submatrix sq mean bins 9 86 0 1 submatrix sq mean / log10 10 * 20 > . cr   \ 1 (14-28 kHz band over 100 Hz-1 kHz band)
silence-audio clear

\ errors
{ :high-pass 10 } :filtered instrument-patch!                     \ (below 20 Hz)
{ :high-pass 30000 } :filtered instrument-patch!                  \ (above 20 kHz)
{ :high-pass :low } :filtered instrument-patch!                   \ (not a number)
